>
>Ok, I've got another hack question.  Not nethack, but hack 1.0.2.

I've been playing this a lot lately, since it's all my system's got. I've 
managed to win with all 6 character classes, and I think I know most
everything about this version.

>I've found a ghost pile and picked up a crysknife that was sitting
>in it.  I've heard that a crysknife is the best weapon in the game.
>I also know that everything in a ghost pile is cursed.  So, I wield
>the crysknife and it gets welded to my hand.  Cool.  
>
>But...  does cursed just mean that I can't unwield it (like I would
>ever want to... hah!) or does it also ahve some sort of penalty
>to hit/damage?

No penalties, you just can't unwield it.  If you ever do uncurse it
(either with a remove curse or enchant weapon scroll), make sure you 
never unwield it without killing something with it first, otherwise
it will turn back into a worm tooth.
 
>Also, I was blinded by something and have been blind for quite a while.
>It's not a big problem since I've eaten a floating eye corpse, but
>I'm wondering if there's some monster out there that can make you
>permanently blind or if I'm just having a bit of bad luck.

You ran into a yellow light.  Just wait a while, you'll get your sight
back.  Nothing in the game will permanently blind you.

>Let's see...  what else...  Does regeneration make you use up food
>faster as it does in some other games?

Yes, quite a bit faster.

>What exactly does royal
>jelly do?  I found a bunch of it in the same ghost pile.

In addition to acting like normal food, royal jelly will sometimes
increase your strength if you eat it.

>Or, does anyone know where the spoilers for this version of hack are?

Nope, but feel free to e-mail me with any other questions.

